  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Making Pregnncy Safer MPS in Amhara ll</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women in Ethiopia often risk their lives when giving birth. Though half of maternal deaths could be prevented if women delivered their babies with a skilled birth attendant, only 10% of women get help from a trained health worker, against a national target of 62%. Access to health services is poor and the standards of health care are low. The distance and the cost to reach health facilities prevent women from getting skilled care. Family planning is the most cost-effective way of reducing maternal deaths but many women in Ethiopia do not use modern family planning methods. This project will increase the number of women that deliver in health centres and use family planning services. It will increase the demand for these services using educational films and other health promotion activities. The project will help communities set up savings groups to pay for transport for medical emergencies. It will train health workers and provide medical equipment to improve the quality of health care. As a result, the project will reduce the number of women and newborns that die.</narrative>
  </description>
